  "term": "Eskalith",
  "definition": "Eskalith refers to lithium carbonate, a lithium salt with mood-stabilizing and antimanic effects. Its exact mood-related action is not fully established, but it affects nerve-cell sodium transport, neurotransmitter release, cellular signaling, and inositol metabolism.",
